 "measuredAtCommit": "re-measured 2026-08-13 at the DR-001 route commit (post C-D005: v1.9 applied, R-1 register repair, freeze register-digest lines refreshed). Drifted sources updated: IMPLEMENTATION-FREEZE.md, claim-register.v1.json. The r1 applied head v1.9 and its chain (v1.8, v1.7; v1.6 already pinned) added this measure. Disposition: MEASURED, pending the re-record reviewer's route verification. | re-measured 2026-08-13 at the turn-2 clearance commit (matrix R-1 row moved to the applied v1.9 pair; v1.9 review pinned as the 40th evidence entry; register currentReviewArtifacts updated). | final sync 2026-08-13: freeze register-lines moved to the post-clearance register digest; pins re-moved; this is the terminal state for the SATISFIED re-record (the row edit touches neither freeze nor register). | re-measured 2026-08-13 at C-D014 (the EVIDENCE application): drifted sources updated: IMPLEMENTER-BLUEPRINT.md, IMPLEMENTATION-FREEZE.md -- both moved by this same commit (freeze section 3 rider, blueprint section 1.1 applied-head row). evidence.v15 and its chain (v14, v13, v12, v11) added; sources now 49. Disposition: MEASURED, not a SATISFIED re-record -- DR-001 re-opens by its own scope clause and its re-record is sequenced before C-final. | re-measured 2026-08-14 at the post-D-044/D-046 HEAD (parent cf1c956). This commit is the MEASURED regeneration D-001 MF-8 and D-044 clauses 3-4 require. Source pins: 49/49 still match live bytes; no path added or dropped; freeze and blueprint unchanged. D-044/D-045/D-046 moved file 08, COORD, and file 09, none of which is a baseline source. Disposition: MEASURED, not SATISFIED. SATISFIED re-record remains a later independently reviewed file-08-only act.",
 "appliedHeadNote": "retention-tiers.v28 (applied head, added this regeneration with its resolution base retention-tiers.v26) resolves by applying its declared operations over v26's REVIEWED BYTES in one hop -- freeze \u00a77.3's terminus rule: v26 is a full-text standalone whose narrative change-log both resolvers misread as a declaration, so full-chain recursion through it refuses by a recorded corpus-level instrument finding (RT28-RES-08 class), not by any defect of v28. Verified this regeneration: 8/8 operations at 0 errors, resolved canonical 4241f87b\u2026 matching the freeze row. evidence-identity-recipes.v12 (applied head, added with its full chain to the v5 terminus) resolves full-chain at 0 errors, canonical 872883db\u2026. | evidence.v15 (applied head 2026-08-13, D-014, added this regeneration with its full chain v14/v13/v12/v11 to the v10 terminus already pinned at /sources/20) resolves FULL-CHAIN at 0 errors under both resolvers -- 20 declared operations over five links -- to canonical 4976151e6ccfd6fd25487e2ebf9e20af3b971e5bc4879b66f11b11c43ba3c573. Note the contrast with retention-tiers.v28 above: that head requires the one-hop terminus rule because full-chain recursion refuses; this head is its exact inverse -- full-chain resolves and a one-hop application over v10 refuses at 3 errors. Neither may be resolved by the other's route."
